 "notes": "Claude first pass. Recurrent deep decels (nadirs 60-100) every 2-3 min from -46 to delivery; classic evolving pattern for pH 7.16. d1 typed early (gradual, mirrors c22, nadir-lag +16s) - borderline vs late, flag for review. All others typed variable on abrupt/jagged morphology; d6-d9 carry the UC flag (toco lost -26..-16). Added contraction cm39 (-27.1..-26.15): clear toco hump the detector missed, it is the contraction linked to d5. Terminal 9 min: baseline estimate collapses to ~95 while true baseline is ~130-140, so shipped depth/lag features there are unreliable; the -9..-6 stretch (d12+d13 with only partial recovery between) is arguably one prolonged complex - kept detector delineation, noted for reviewer. Tail after -2.6 sits ~100 with no further discrete decels.",
